    "implementation": [
      "Add generic current-meeting metadata scope and commitment/proposal/scope/limitation instructions as a separate v2 constant. No new source context, heuristics, normalization, truncation, label rewriting, or decision postprocessing.",
      "ScopedBatchedAnalysisGenerator uses inherited classify_bounded loop unchanged except policy-selected messages and metadata. batch_messages defaults to original v1. All parser, grammar, per-batch input admission, cap8/output128/EOS, no retry/partial return and cache policies retained.",
      "Service explicitly maps single/v1/v2 to normal or observer generator; v2 observer MRO reuses existing hooks. Actual generator policy determines health and shared outer deadline; requested versus loaded policy mismatch and runtime policy drift fail closed.",
      "Both launchers and acceptance driver reuse existing shared POLICIES, CLI argument forwarding, health equality, lifecycle and explicit registration/code/CI/same-policy calibration gates. Those three production files remain byte-identical; their tests add v2 and cross-policy cases.",
      "Frozen metadata literal parsing and strict conflict checks unchanged. Identical current-meeting metadata repeats preserve both original evidence spans; distinct values still fail. Summary remains extractive."
    ],
